{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1098305-new-player-lf-demon-game","id":1098305,"title":"New Player LF Demon Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-29T18:25:41-07:00","id":1098305,"title":"New Player LF Demon Game","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I'm interested in playing a game of Demon: The Descent, but don't know anyone in my immediate vicinity with much roleplaying experience.<br /> <br /> For this reason, I thought I'd seek out a game on the official forums.<br /> <br /> I'm basically looking for an already assembled group I can join--preferably with an experienced Storyteller--so that things run fairly smoothly and I can learn the game play mechanics alongside people who are already acquainted with them rather than having to go through the difficult process of repeatedly looking them up and/or learning them in the company of other novices.<br /> <br /> I have a copy of the core rulebook (from the original Kickstarter release), a copy of the <u>God Machine Chronicle</u>, and the set of condition cards associated with the game. It's possible I could download, purchase, or otherwise obtain <u>Flowers of Hell</u> and any other supplementary materials the group might be using.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm looking for a reasonably mature, established roleplaying group with experience playing within any of the myriad White Wolf/Onyx Path (Classic World of Darkness and/or Chronicles of Darkness) settings. <br /> <br /> I'm primarily interested in Demon because of its relative novelty, but would be interested in trying out virtually any of the other games released by White Wolf over the years. I've accumulated a rather sizable collection of books and materials associated with various games, have perused through them, read some of the Vampire: The Masquerade clan novels, and played both VtM:Redemption and VtM:Bloodlines. But I've never actually played any of the pen and paper games.<br /> <br /> My intention is to leave this post up for roughly a week or so to see what replies I garner before moving on to post in other forums associated with other games.<br /> <br /> I appreciate any replies or invites people send my way.<br /> <br /> Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13431-gentle_rain","name":"Gentle_Rain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T23:04:55-07:00","id":1098668,"title":"","content":"Great advert, wrong thread for it;<br /> <br /> The thread you want is here, on the Conventions, Gatherings and Online Play area. It's where I found a couple of GMs, both very good, though it's by no means guaranteed you'll find a game: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...and-gatherings</a><br /> <br /> Best of luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 05-31-2017, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T06:03:53-07:00","id":1098741,"title":"","content":"Hey I have a game that could use one more player","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"re